      "css": ":host{--m0:#0D0716;--m3:#641A80;--m4:#8C2981;--m5:#B73779;--m6:#DE4968;--m8:#FE9F6D;--m9:#FECF92;--field:#0D0716;--field-ink:#F6EFF4;--field-ink-2:#D8C9DD;--field-muted:#A898B1;--field-rule:rgba(252,253,191,.14);--ground:#FAF9FB;--ink:#1A1024;--ink-2:#44384F;--muted:#675B71;--rule:#E2DDE8;--rule-strong:#C9C0D3;--r:2px;--sans:'Archivo',ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;--mono:'Martian Mono',ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;--ease-out:cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1);font-family:var(--sans);} .ds-field2{background:var(--field);padding:32px;} .ds-mail{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;padding:16px 18px;border:1px solid var(--field-rule);border-radius:var(--r);font-family:var(--mono);font-stretch:75%;font-size:1rem;} .ds-mail a{color:var(--field-ink);text-decoration:none;} .ds-mail a:hover{color:var(--m9);} .ds-copy{margin-left:auto;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.82rem;font-weight:600;padding:7px 12px;min-height:36px;border-radius:var(--r);border:1px solid var(--field-rule);background:transparent;color:var(--field-ink-2);cursor:pointer;} .ds-copy:hover{color:var(--field-ink);border-color:var(--field-muted);} .ds-copy:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--m9);outline-offset:3px;}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Behavior Map",
    "overview": "The site reads like a behavior-space density map. A dark field of smooth magma heat, thin contour lines and a dust of points sits at the top of every page; the work is organized into four labeled regions (C1 Model the data, C2 Build the tool, C3 Design the study, C4 Test the cause), and that one cluster-ID labeling system tags every project and paper. On the home page the points start as uniform noise and settle into the clusters once; under reduced motion the settled map draws at once. Hovering or focusing a key lights its region and every item tagged with it across the page (linked brushing).\n\nBelow the field, reading happens on cool plot-paper white, or on the field's own black in the dark theme. Structure comes from hairline rules and grid rows, not containers: lists of regions, works, papers and timeline entries are ruled rows. Figures are numbered and captioned (\"Fig. 1\", \"Fig. 2\") the way a paper's are, and every chart is an original drawing or a design schematic.\n\nThe density is calm: generous band padding, one idea per band, short ruled rows. The world refuses the portfolio template (name hero beside a portrait, stats strip, icon-card grid, chip clouds, kickers) and the faculty CV.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One colormap (magma) supplies every color, including the four cluster colors.",
      "A dark map field anchors every page top (map hero on home, point-cloud page head inside) and the closing band and footer.",
      "Archivo variable width for all reading text; Martian Mono only for IDs, axes, DOIs, years and counts.",
      "Square 2px corners, hairline rules, no elevation.",
      "Cluster keys (colored dot plus ID and name) are the single labeling system site-wide, and they drive linked brushing."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Colormap Rule",
        "body": "No color enters the system that is not a magma sample or a magma-tinted neutral. A new accent is a new magma stop, not a new hue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Cluster Color Is a Key Rule",
        "body": "Cluster colors only identify a region (dots, bullets, underlines, lit points). They never fill buttons, backgrounds or text.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Field Is Always Dark Rule",
        "body": "The map field, page heads, closing band and footer use the Field tokens in both themes; only reading surfaces switch.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Mono Is For Values Rule",
        "body": "Martian Mono sets only IDs, axes, DOIs, years, dates, counts and figure numbers. Cluster names, flags, readout labels and all prose are Archivo.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Meta Below Rule",
        "body": "No kicker or eyebrow above a heading. Meta lines (version, status, role) sit directly below the heading they describe.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Field Is the Depth Rule",
        "body": "Surfaces never lift. To separate, use a hairline, a tinted band, or the dark field.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Points Are Round Rule",
        "body": "Round shapes mean data points or cluster keys. Containers stay square.",
        "section": "shapes"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** take every new color from magma or the magma-tinted neutrals.",
      "**Do** tag projects and papers with cluster keys (dot, mono ID, Archivo name) and wire them to linked brushing.",
      "**Do** set IDs, axes, DOIs, years, dates and counts in Martian Mono at width 75, and everything else in Archivo.",
      "**Do** put small labels in expanded tracked Archivo caps (width 118 to 125, .1 to .16em).",
      "**Do** place meta lines (version, status, role) below the heading.",
      "**Do** caption figures with a mono \"Fig. N\" and keep charts original or schematic.",
      "**Do** gate JS-dependent hiding on the live state (`.mapfig.is-live`, `.js`) so the page reads fully without JavaScript.",
      "**Do** make every motion static under prefers-reduced-motion.",
      "**Do** flex a page's single field band down to the footer."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** add kickers or eyebrows above headings.",
      "**Don't** lift surfaces with drop shadows or use cards as structure; text halos on the field and brushing rings on cluster dots are the only shadows.",
      "**Don't** color text or fills with cluster colors; cluster color lives in the dot.",
      "**Don't** set names, flags, labels or prose in Martian Mono.",
      "**Don't** round containers past 2px.",
      "**Don't** build portfolio tropes: a name hero beside a portrait, stats strips, icon-card grids, chip clouds."
    ]
  }
}